17:## Global style
34:## Frame 1 — Hook: nobody keeps score
36:- status: outline
37:- src: compositions/01-hook.html
38:- duration: 17s
39:- start: 0.0s
40:- transition_in: cut
41:- scene: Typeset cold open. A single statistic fills the frame, then a thin accent rule draws under it.
42:- voiceover: "In 2015, Indonesia's peat fires released more carbon dioxide per day than the entire United States economy. That is a World Resources Institute analysis of the Global Fire Emissions Database. Every dry season, fire commanders act on those forecasts, and nobody keeps score of them."
43:- poster: 6s
44:- audio: audio/scene-01-hook.aiff
74:## Frame 2 — The problem: fragmented and unverifiable
76:- status: outline
77:- src: compositions/02-problem.html
78:- duration: 19s
79:- start: 17.0s
80:- transition_in: crossfade
81:- scene: Same canvas as Frame 1. A headline, three chips, and a diagram whose last link is dashed and empty.
82:- voiceover: "This is a Climate Data and Environmental Monitoring track build, and the problem is familiar: environmental data is fragmented and hard to verify. You cannot prove what a model said before the fire spread. And a model can always be tuned until the past looks good. So nobody knows which forecasts deserve trust."
83:- poster: 8s
84:- audio: audio/scene-02-problem.aiff
113:## Frame 3 — What it does: one forecast from live open data
115:- status: outline
116:- src: compositions/03-what-it-does.html
117:- duration: 25s
118:- start: 36.0s
119:- transition_in: crossfade
120:- scene: Four live data sources feed one grid. A drawn arrow carries the eye to an 8×8 cell grid where a few cells catch fire.
121:- voiceover: "SekatApi joins live open data into one fire-spread forecast. NASA FIRMS satellite hotspots for where fire is now. Open-Meteo for wind, humidity and rain. AWS terrain for slope. OpenStreetMap for rivers and roads. It runs on a six point four by six point four kilometre grid at one hundred metre cells, forty simulated runs, twenty four to forty eight hours ahead. You see the uncertainty, not one confident line."
122:- poster: 12s
123:- audio: audio/scene-03-what-it-does.aiff
