162:- status: outline
163:- src: compositions/04-recorded-fire.html
164:- duration: 27s
165:- start: 61.0s
166:- transition_in: crossfade
167:- scene: Real app screenshot with a slow push; an accent outline lands on the score card. Then a cut to the live-fires sheet beside a big count.
168:- voiceover: "Here is a real West Kalimantan fire, frozen at the last satellite pass on the eighteenth of October, twenty twenty six. The next day the satellites found eighteen new fire spots. The forecast caught twelve: a critical success index of point four one, against point one seven for a distance-only baseline. The white rings are what the satellites saw. Live, Kalimantan shows two thousand four hundred fifty two detections in the last day."
169:- poster: 10s
170:- audio: audio/scene-04-recorded-fire.aiff
209:## Frame 5 — Honest validation: the hindcast
211:- status: outline
212:- src: compositions/05-hindcast.html
213:- duration: 33s
214:- start: 88.0s
215:- transition_in: cut
216:- scene: Two honest bar charts side by side, then a third strip that shows the first model over-forecasting six times too much.
217:- voiceover: "Now the honest part. We hindcast twelve real fires, eight to eighteen October. The first model spread about six times too much fire: a score of point one seven, no better than a distance-only baseline at point one six. We slowed the spread, choosing the parameter on Kalimantan only. On held-out Sumatra, the score moved from point zero eight to point one one, against point zero nine. Pooled over all twelve: point two two against point one seven. Small — we say so. Re-running it a day later gave identical counts."
218:- poster: 18s
219:- audio: audio/scene-05-hindcast.aiff
